## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical multi-tenant streaming design, data contracts, lineage, schema evolution, late data, and engine trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Per-record contracts and schema registry
- Per-record lineage in metadata store
- Late data handling and watermarks
- Idempotent upserts into Iceberg
- Tenant isolation and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Contract check example (pseudo)
function validate(record, contract){
  for (const f of contract.fields){
    if (f.required && (record[f.name] === undefined || record[f.name] === null)) return false;
    // type checks omitted for brevity
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement a governance layer for schema evolution across tenants?
- What tests would you add to guard against drift in late-arriving records?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable data lifecycle with multi-tenant governance and cost control; integrates Iceberg features, storage tiering, policy-driven retention, and query-layer masking.

## Key Concepts
- Iceberg time travel via snapshots
- Dynamic data tiering (hot/warm/cold)
- Per-tenant data masking
- Encryption at rest (KMS)
- Partition pruning and metadata caching

## Code Example
```javascript
function selectTier(tenant, ageDays) {
  const retention = (tenantRetention[tenant] || 365);
  if (ageDays < 30) return 'hot';
  if (ageDays < retention) return 'warm';
  return 'cold';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test data freshness and mask correctness across tiers?
- How would you validate time travel remains accurate after tiering moves?
